# Reqly's desktop file, named after its app ID, which GTK gives its window on Wayland and as its
# X11 class, so docks and task bars show Reqly's name and icon. For checks in a desktop VM, with
# `reqly` on PATH; linux/README.md says how to install it there. Reqly doesn't open files yet, so
# MimeType, with Reqly's own file types, and the action that starts capturing come with the package.
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Reqly
Comment=See what your apps send and receive
Exec=reqly %F
Icon=net.reqly.Reqly
Categories=Development;Network;
Keywords=proxy;http;https;traffic;har;debug;
StartupNotify=true
StartupWMClass=net.reqly.Reqly
